---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="About Umut Sevinç (VulnSVNC) | Turkey-based Vulnerability Researcher"
  description="Umut Sevinç (VulnSVNC) is a Turkey-based vulnerability researcher and offensive security analyst publishing CVEs in security tooling."
  path="/en/about"
  alternates={[{ hreflang: 'tr', path: '/tr/hakkinda' }, { hreflang: 'en', path: '/en/about' }]}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-50">Umut Sevinç (VulnSVNC) <span class="block text-emerald-400 text-xl mt-1">Turkey-based Vulnerability Researcher</span></h1>

  <section class="mt-6 space-y-3 max-w-3xl">
    <p>
      Umut Sevinç (VulnSVNC, also written Umut SEVİNÇ) is a vulnerability researcher and offensive security analyst based in Türkiye.
      Areas of work: {SITE.expertise.join(', ')}.
    </p>
    <p>Community and education roles: {SITE.communities.join(', ')}.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="meta">
    <h2 id="meta" class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50">Research approach: security of offensive tooling</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Much of the research targets vulnerabilities in the offensive security tools that practitioners rely on. Because these tools
      process untrusted network input, memory corruption and command injection bugs in them can put the operator at risk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="disclosure">
    <h2 id="disclosure" class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50">Responsible disclosure</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Issues are reported to the vendor or maintainer first.</li>
      <li>CVE IDs are requested through coordinated disclosure (e.g. the VulnCheck CNA).</li>
      <li>Details are published with the CVE record after a patch or a reasonable disclosure window.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-8"><a class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline" href="/#cves">→ Published CVE records</a></p>
</Base>
